for-differentials-of-smooth-maps":"mathematical-premise"},"inventory_expansion_required":false,"statement":"Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, and let $\\pi:P\\to M$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle for a finite-dimensional real Lie group $G$, with $\\mathfrak g=\\operatorname{Lie}(G)=T_eG$. A supplied principal connection is a smooth, right-invariant complement $TP=VP\\oplus H$, where $VP=\\ker d\\pi$; write $v:TP\\to VP$ for the projection along $H$, and let $K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY])$ be its vertical-valued curvature. For $Z\\in\\mathfrak g$ and $p\\in P$, define the fundamental vertical vector $Z_P(p)=\\left.\\frac{d}{dt}\\right|_{t=0}p\\exp_G(tZ)$. The orbit differential $\\zeta_p: \\mathfrak g\\to V_pP$, $Z\\mapsto Z_P(p)$, is a linear isomorphism, as proved below. Define the **principal connection 1-form** by\n\n$$\\omega_p(X):=\\zeta_p^{-1}(v_pX),\\qquad X\\in T_pP.$$\n\nThen $\\omega$ is a smooth $\\mathfrak g$-valued 1-form satisfying $\\omega(Z_P)=Z$, $\\ker\\omega=H$, and $R_g^*\\omega=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g^{-1}}\\omega$ for every fixed $g\\in G$. Conversely, a smooth $\\mathfrak g$-valued 1-form with the reproduction and equivariance properties determines the principal connection $H=\\ker\\omega$. The converted vertical curvature $\\kappa_H:=\\omega\\circ K_H$ is a $\\mathfrak g$-valued alternating 2-form; its equality with the Cartan curvature is established in the curvature lemma.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§1.3.1, printed pp. 32–35: fundamental vertical vectors, the isomorphism with the vertical bundle, reproduction, equivariance, and the connection 1-form."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf","locator":"Chapter 5, §5.4, printed pp. 92–94: connection 1-form axioms, reconstruction of the horizontal distribution, and variable gauge transitions."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"direct"},{"id":"def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket","kind":"definition","domain":"mathematics","title":"Graded bracket of Lie-algebra-valued differential forms","reference":"items/def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored; authorized inventory expansion recorded; readiness recording follows final scoped checks.","dependency_level":0,"deps":["def-finite-dimensional-lie-algebra","def-finite-dimensional-vector-valued-forms-and-their-exterior-derivative","def-wedge-product-of-differential-forms","prop-differential-forms-form-a-graded-commutative-algebra","thm-the-exterior-derivative-is-a-graded-derivation"],"dependency_roles":{"def-finite-dimensional-lie-algebra":"mathematical-premise","def-finite-dimensional-vector-valued-forms-and-their-exterior-derivative":"mathematical-premise","def-wedge-product-of-differential-forms":"mathematical-premise","prop-differential-forms-form-a-graded-commutative-algebra":"mathematical-premise","thm-the-exterior-derivative-is-a-graded-derivation":"mathematical-premise"},"inventory_expansion_required":true,"statement":"Let $M$ be a smooth manifold and $\\mathfrak g$ a finite-dimensional real Lie algebra. For homogeneous $\\alpha\\in\\Omega^p(M,\\mathfrak g)$ and $\\beta\\in\\Omega^q(M,\\mathfrak g)$, define their **graded bracket** by\n\n$$[\\alpha\\wedge\\beta](X_1,\\ldots,X_{p+q}) := \\frac{1}{p!q!}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in S_{p+q}}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\sigma)[\\alpha(X_{\\sigma(1)},\\ldots,X_{\\sigma(p)}),\\beta(X_{\\sigma(p+1)},\\ldots,X_{\\sigma(p+q)})].$$\n\nHere $\\Omega^p(M,\\mathfrak g)$ is the space of smooth alternating $p$-linear forms with values in $\\mathfrak g$, the inner bracket is the Lie-algebra bracket, and the sum is over all permutations. This is a smooth $\\mathfrak g$-valued $(p+q)$-form. It obeys graded skew-symmetry $[\\alpha\\wedge\\beta]=-(-1)^{pq}[\\beta\\wedge\\alpha]$, graded Jacobi\n\n$$\\left[\\alpha\\wedge\\left[\\beta\\wedge\\gamma\\right]\\right]=\\left[\\left[\\alpha\\wedge\\beta\\right]\\wedge\\gamma\\right]+(-1)^{pq}\\left[\\beta\\wedge\\left[\\alpha\\wedge\\gamma\\right]\\right],$$\n\nand the exterior-derivative rule\n\n$$d[\\alpha\\wedge\\beta]=[d\\alpha\\wedge\\beta]+(-1)^p[\\alpha\\wedge d\\beta].$$\n\nIn particular, for $\\mathfrak g$-valued 1-forms $A,B$, $[A\\wedge B](X,Y)=[A(X),B(Y)]-[A(Y),B(X)]$, so $\\tfrac12[A\\wedge A](X,Y)=[A(X),A(Y)]$. This fixes the normalization used by the Cartan curvature formula.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§1.3.1, printed pp. 34–35: the graded bracket of Lie-algebra-valued forms and its graded Leibniz rule."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf","locator":"Chapter 6 §6.1, printed pp. 100–101: bracket convention, Cartan curvature formula, and curvature equivariance."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"direct"},{"id":"lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi","kind":"lemma","domain":"mathematics","title":"Principal curvature, Cartan structure equation, and Bianchi identity","reference":"items/lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored; readiness recording follows final scoped checks.","dependency_level":1,"deps":["def-countable-choice","def-qftx-principal-connection-form","def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket","def-principal-connection-and-vertical-curvature","def-smooth-principal-g-bundle","def-lie-group","thm-the-tangent-space-at-the-identity-is-a-lie-algebra","def-adjoint-representation-of-a-lie-algebra","def-conjugation-and-the-adjoint-representation-of-a-lie-gro