exterior-derivative":"mathematical-premise","thm-the-exterior-derivative-commutes-with-pullback":"mathematical-premise","thm-the-exterior-derivative-squares-to-zero":"mathematical-premise"},"inventory_expansion_required":false,"statement":"Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, and let $\\pi:P\\to M$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle with a principal connection form $\\omega$ associated to $H$, using $Z_P(p)=\\left.\\frac{d}{dt}\\right|_0p\\exp_G(tZ)$ for the right action. For Lie-algebra-valued forms use the graded bracket defined by alternating shuffle and the Lie bracket; in degree one, $[A\\wedge B](X,Y)=[A(X),B(Y)]-[A(Y),B(X)]$. Define\n\n$$\\Omega_\\omega:=d\\omega+\\frac12[\\omega\\wedge\\omega],\\qquad D_\\omega\\eta:=d\\eta+[\\omega\\wedge\\eta].$$\n\nThen $\\Omega_\\omega$ is horizontal and $\\operatorname{Ad}$-equivariant, and $\\Omega_\\omega=\\omega\\circ K_H$ for the imported vertical-valued curvature $K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY])$. For any trivializing cover with smooth sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=s_i^*\\Omega_\\omega$. On an overlap, let $g_{ij}:U_i\\cap U_j\\to G$ be the smooth map determined by $s_j=s_i g_{ij}$, and write $\\theta_L(g_{ij})=g_{ij}^*\\theta_L$ for the left Maurer–Cartan form. Then\n\n$$A_j=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+\\theta_L(g_{ij}),\\qquad F_i=dA_i+\\frac12[A_i\\wedge A_i],\\qquad F_j=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}F_i,\\qquad D_{A_i}F_i=0,$$\n\nwhere $D_{A_i}\\eta:=d\\eta+[A_i\\wedge\\eta]$. The transition equations concern changes of local sections; they do not identify an arbitrary map $M\\to G$ with a global automorphism of a nontrivial bundle.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§1.3.1, printed pp. 32–36: Cartan’s second structure equation, curvature horizontality/equivariance, Bianchi identity, and the local gauge convention."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf","locator":"Chapter 5 §5.4, printed pp. 92–95, and Chapter 6 §6.1, printed pp. 100–101: connection forms, local transition law, curvature type, and local Cartan formula."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"direct"},{"id":"def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative","kind":"definition","domain":"mathematics","title":"Covariant derivative on an associated representation bundle","reference":"items/def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored; readiness recording follows final scoped checks.","dependency_level":1,"deps":["def-countable-choice","def-qftx-principal-connection-form","def-smooth-principal-g-bundle","def-finite-dimensional-representation-of-a-group-over-a-field","def-associated-bundle-to-a-principal-bundle-and-representation","thm-associated-vector-bundle-is-well-defined","def-differential-of-a-smooth-map","thm-chain-rule-for-differentials-of-smooth-maps","def-left-maurer-cartan-form","def-conjugation-and-the-adjoint-representation-of-a-lie-group","def-exponential-map-of-a-lie-group","thm-one-parameter-subgroups-are-integral-curves-of-left-invariant-fields"],"dependency_roles":{"def-countable-choice":"mathematical-premise","def-qftx-principal-connection-form":"mathematical-premise","def-smooth-principal-g-bundle":"mathematical-premise","def-finite-dimensional-representation-of-a-group-over-a-field":"mathematical-premise","def-associated-bundle-to-a-principal-bundle-and-representation":"mathematical-premise","thm-associated-vector-bundle-is-well-defined":"mathematical-premise","def-differential-of-a-smooth-map":"mathematical-premise","thm-chain-rule-for-differentials-of-smooth-maps":"mathematical-premise","def-left-maurer-cartan-form":"mathematical-premise","def-conjugation-and-the-adjoint-representation-of-a-lie-group":"mathematical-premise","def-exponential-map-of-a-lie-group":"mathematical-premise","thm-one-parameter-subgroups-are-integral-curves-of-left-invariant-fields":"mathematical-premise"},"inventory_expansion_required":false,"statement":"Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $M$ be a finite-dimensional smooth manifold, $G$ a finite-dimensional real Lie group, $\\pi:P\\to M$ a smooth right principal $G$-bundle, and $\\omega$ the principal connection 1-form of a supplied horizontal distribution. Fix a finite-dimensional complex representation $\\rho:G\\to\\operatorname{GL}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$ that is smooth, and let $E=P\\times_\\rho V$ be its associated vector bundle with relation $[pg,v]=[p,\\rho(g)v]$. Define $\\rho_*:=d\\rho_e:\\mathfrak g\\to\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$, where the differential is taken after viewing $\\rho$ as a smooth matrix-valued map. For any open cover with smooth local sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, write $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$. A smooth section $\\sigma$ of $E$ has unique local components $\\psi_i:U_i\\to V$ given by $\\sigma(x)=[s_i(x),\\psi_i(x)]$. Define the **associated covariant derivative** $\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ by its local components\n\n$$\n(\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma)_i=d\\psi_i+\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i,\n$$\n\nwhere $(\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i)(X)=\\rho_*(A_i(X))\\psi_i$ for $X\\in TU_i$. These expressions patch to a smooth $E$-valued 1-form on $M$, independently of the chosen local sections, and satisfy $\\nabla^\\omega(f\\sigma)=df\\otimes\\sigma+f\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ for every smooth scalar function $f$ on $M$.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Matthijs Vákár, Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories (full text)","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334","locator":"§§1.3.3 and 1.4.1, printed pp. 37–42: the induced associated connection, local covariant derivative, and Leibniz rule."},{"title":"Karl-Hermann Neeb, Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles (full lecture notes, 2024)","url":"https://ww