      "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $M$ be a finite-dimensional smooth manifold, $G$ a finite-dimensional real Lie group, $\\pi:P\\to M$ a smooth right principal $G$-bundle, and $\\omega$ the principal connection 1-form of a supplied horizontal distribution. Fix a finite-dimensional complex representation $\\rho:G\\to\\operatorname{GL}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$ that is smooth, and let $E=P\\times_\\rho V$ be its associated vector bundle with relation $[pg,v]=[p,\\rho(g)v]$. Define $\\rho_*:=d\\rho_e:\\mathfrak g\\to\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$, where the differential is taken after viewing $\\rho$ as a smooth matrix-valued map. For any open cover with smooth local sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, write $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$. A smooth section $\\sigma$ of $E$ has unique local components $\\psi_i:U_i\\to V$ given by $\\sigma(x)=[s_i(x),\\psi_i(x)]$. Define the **associated covariant derivative** $\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ by its local components\n\n$$\n(\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma)_i=d\\psi_i+\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i,\n$$\n\nwhere $(\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i)(X)=\\rho_*(A_i(X))\\psi_i$ for $X\\in TU_i$. These expressions patch to a smooth $E$-valued 1-form on $M$, independently of the chosen local sections, and satisfy $\\nabla^\\omega(f\\sigma)=df\\otimes\\sigma+f\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ for every smooth scalar function $f$ on $M$.",
