+# Batch 37 — Step 1 authoring evidence
+
+Run: advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23  
+Scope: qftx-p-form-symmetries and its examples companion.
+
+## Scope and plan reconciliation
+
+Read the assigned beta task, owner authoring direction, complete design section at research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md under “Topological Defects and Interfaces” and “Higher-Form Symmetries and Charge Operators,” the matching rows in research/plan-spec.json, the current batch-37 manifest, the complete run dependency-level file, the assigned item contract, the generalized-symmetry specialist note, and the complete prose scaffold.
+
+The design and canonical plan agree exactly on A/B IDs, title, category, physics library, order 993, companion, and A-page prerequisites qftx-defects-and-topological-operators and qftx-gauge-geometry. The B page depends on the A page. Both plan rows have empty item arrays. The owner direction explicitly says these arrays are planning placeholders and requires substantive B-page examples, so this batch fills its assigned manifests and pages without changing the shared plan. No design/plan conflict was found.
+
+The assigned planned contract is def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry: a group-like p-form symmetry with exact support, charge and background conventions in a selected d-dimensional model. The A page adds the local conditional theorem pthm-aqft-p-form-charge-characters because the Pontryagin-dual character claim needs a complete exchange and scalar-action argument. The B page contains a compact-U(1) magnetic one-form example and a finite S3 zero-form representation comparison. Neither example claims a continuum path-integral construction or reports an experiment.
+
+## Dependency inventory, actual suppliers, and levels
+
+The current dependency-level record places batch 37 at level 4 with required batches 2 and 36; batch 2 is level 0 and batch 36 is level 3. The assigned A-page prerequisites remain those exact pages.
+
+| Item | Direct in-run item suppliers | Item level | Current disposition |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry | def-aqft-topological-interface (batch 36, level 1) | 2 | Complete conditional definition; escalated because the supplier's current Step 1 record is missing. |
+| pthm-aqft-p-form-charge-characters | def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry | 3 | Complete proof of the group exchange and simple-character conclusions; inherits the unresolved interface readiness. |
+| ex-aqft-maxwell-magnetic-one-form-charge | def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry, pthm-aqft-p-form-charge-characters; plus batch-2 mathematical suppliers def-qftx-principal-connection-form (level 0) and lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi (level 1) | 4 | Complete conditional flux/charge calculation; gauge-geometry suppliers are current and ready, while interface readiness is unresolved transitively. |
+| ex-aqft-s3-zero-form-representation-labels | def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry, pthm-aqft-p-form-charge-characters | 4 | Complete finite representation calculation; inherits the unresolved interface readiness. |
+
+Before authoring, loadStep1Record and step1Decision were run against the live frontier. The exact current def-aqft-topological-interface and def-aqft-topological-defect carriers both exist and were read completely, but are not yet listed in the current batch-36 manifest and each has no current Step 1 readiness record. The topological-interface definition states the same-complete-model, two-sided inverse, and observable/background-preserving requirements used here. Draft status and precheck state were not treated as scientific defects; the unresolved item is the fresh missing authoring-readiness record and owner manifest inventory. The consumer arguments are completed conditionally, retained with the actual supplier dependencies, and marked escalated. Batch 36 remains owner of these carriers.
+
+The current qftx-gauge-geometry mathematical A page contains the exact right-principal-connection and curvature/Bianchi suppliers used by the Maxwell example. Its def-qftx-principal-connection-form and lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi carriers and complete proofs were inspected; their current Step 1 records are ready. The exact conventions are a smooth right principal bundle, right action, curvature K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY]), local F_i=dA_i+1/2[A_i∧A_i], and covariant Bianchi D_{A_i}F_i=0. Their inherited axiom is only AC_omega; the Maxwell example states it explicitly and makes the Abelian reduction D_A F=dF.
+
+The Stokes input is the pinned imported mathematical theorem thm-stokes-theorem-for-smooth-singular-chains (local pin SHA256 4ca4ee8333f2ef28244e37e8447a26dc89b38521a63d08ca2f60a815215b16fe). Its full statement and proof were read. It applies to finite smooth singular chains and smooth forms without a choice assumption. The Maxwell proof uses it only after deleting small neighborhoods of the external line's transverse intersections, so the chain lies in the source-free connection domain.
+
+The page-level dependency to qftx-gauge-geometry is verified by that explicit Maxwell use. The page-level dependency to qftx-defects-and-topological-operators and the direct item edge to def-aqft-topological-interface remain open until batch 36 records current readiness. The exact rows are in the JSON cross-batch dependency file. No other batch's supplier was authored or changed.
+
+## Sources read and source dispositions
+
+1. Davide Gaiotto, Anton Kapustin, Nathan Seiberg, and Brian Willett, [Generalized Global Symmetries](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1412.5148), arXiv:1412.5148v2. Read the complete relevant parts of §1 (PDF pp. 1–3), §2 (PDF pp. 5–8), §3 (PDF pp. 11–12), §4.1 (PDF pp. 14–16), and Appendix F (PDF pp. 70–71). These support the group-like defect interface, codimension/support conventions, exchange argument, compact-U(1) magnetic surface and line charge, ordinary zero-form representation action, and the torsion-flux caveat. Appendix F's noncommuting electric/magnetic flux operators are treated as a mixed relation between distinct symmetries, not as a failure of the within-group exchange conclusion.
+2. Lakshya Bhardwaj, Lea E. Bottini, Ludovic Fraser-Taliente, Liam Gladden, Dewi S. W. Gould, Arthur Platschorre, and Hannah Tillim, [Lectures on Generalized Symmetries](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.07547), arXiv:2307.07547v2. Retrieved the full 150-page lecture-notes PDF and read §§2.1 and 2.2.1–2.2.2 (PDF pp. 5–20), including the complete simple-operator crossing/character argument, and §4.1 (PDF pp. 60–62) for continuous and discrete backgrounds. This is the independent full lecture-note treatment. Higher categorical charges for operators of dimension greater than p are explicitly out of scope; higher-group modifications are deferred to qftx-two-group-symmetry-backgrounds.
+
+Every harvested result and its per-item disposition is recorded in research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-37.coverage.json. The original and lecture-note conventions differ by normalization in some Maxwell formulas; the local example fixes holonomy exp(i∫A), F/(2π) integral normalization, and line flux 2πm. No source argument substitutes for the local proofs. Browser inspection succeeded for both full texts; source-fetch-check --stamp remains to be recorded after the coverage manifest is finalized.
+
+## Item progress
+
+- def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry defines the selected model interface, faithful group of codimension-(p+1) invertible topological defects, genuine p-dimensional observables, character notation, finite cochain backgrounds, continuous higher-connection background data, boundary restrictions, and the no-automatic-coupling caveat. Its only direct supplier is the in-run def-aqft-topological-interface (formulation prerequisite); its actual statement is used conditionally. The A definition is uninterrupted and its references follow in Definition references.
+- pthm-aqft-p-form-charge-characters proves group commutativity from the explicit local exchange isotopy and identifies the crossing action on a simple bounded operator as a continuous U(1) character. The scalar/simple, unitary, continuity, faithfulness, and topology hypotheses are explicit. Its proof stands independently of the diagram in Remarks. It depends on the p-form definition at level 3.
+- ex-aqft-maxwell-magnetic-one-form-charge fixes compact U(1), the Euclidean four-dimensional unit convention, curvature normalization, pure-gauge/source assumptions, an external genuine magnetic line with integer linking flux, and the surface character. Its complete conditional proof uses the current connection and Bianchi suppliers plus the pinned smooth-chain Stokes theorem; it neither uses Maxwell's equation of motion nor asserts an empirical result or continuum measure. It is at level 4.
+- ex-aqft-s3-zero-form-representation-labels gives a finite three-state quantum model; its local matrix proof establishes the permutation representation, the noncommuting group elements, and the irreducible trivial-plus-standard decomposition. It distinguishes zero-form representation labels from group elements and is at level 4.
+
+## Authoring and validation state
+
+The assigned A/B page files contain frontmatter only. The shared plan, published content, imports, engine state, and owner verdicts were not edited. Item carriers, run manifest, proof contracts, source coverage, notes, and cross-batch rows are now present.
+
+Pending: source-fetch stamping; the complete scoped format, rendering, provenance, dependency and proof-contract checks; explicit proof-layout checks after final edits; and Step 1 readiness records. The two affected consumers must receive escalated readiness because the exact batch-36 supplier readiness record is missing. No item is marked ready by draft status, citation, or independent-approval label.
+
+Next action: run source-fetch-check with --stamp, resolve any retrieval failure within the five-retry limit, execute the assigned-scope validators, repair formatting or contract defects, recompute item levels, record each readiness decision with actual dependency evidence, and update this note with command results.
