        "statement": "Use natural units $\\hbar=c=1$ and $M=\\mathbb R^4$ with its standard orientation and Euclidean metric. The selected field model is pure compact Maxwell theory with actual gauge group $U(1)=\\{e^{i\\alpha}:\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\mathbb Z\\}$, no dynamical electric or magnetic matter, and a smooth right principal $U(1)$-bundle with connection on the complement of admitted external line insertions. A principal connection is a smooth $\\mathfrak u(1)$-valued one-form reproducing each fundamental vertical vector and equivariant under the right group action. Identify $\\mathfrak u(1)=i\\mathbb R$ with $\\mathbb R$ so its local potentials $A_i$ have holonomy $\\exp(i\\int A_i)$ and the real curvature $F$ obeys $F|_{U_i}=dA_i$, since the Abelian Lie bracket vanishes. The model fixes the action convention $S[A]=(2e^2)^{-1}\\int F\\wedge *F$ with dimensionless $e>0$, integrating outside any prescribed line-core tube with its declared boundary condition. It also fixes the allowed bundle sectors, boundary behavior at infinity, and any regulator or measure; no continuum measure is constructed here. With this normalization $[A_i]=\\mathrm{length}^{-1}$, $[F]=\\mathrm{length}^{-2}$, and $\\int_\\Sigma F$ is dimensionless.\n\nLet $C$ be a closed smooth oriented curve carrying an admitted genuine external magnetic line $T_m(C)$, where genuine means that no auxiliary surface is attached to define the insertion. Its integer charge $m\\in\\mathbb Z$ is specified by $\\int_{S^2_{\\mathrm{link}}}F=2\\pi m$ on every sufficiently small oriented normal two-sphere linking $C$. The model has no other magnetic sources, and its normalized correlation functional is assumed to be defined for these insertions.\n\nFor a closed smooth oriented surface $\\Sigma$ disjoint from the line, and $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\mathbb Z$, define the magnetic surface operator\n\n$$\nU_\\alpha(\\Sigma)=\\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{i\\alpha}{2\\pi}\\int_\\Sigma F\\right).\n$$\n\nFor this example, a smooth singular three-chain is a finite real linear combination of smooth maps from the standard 3-simplex, with boundary the alternating sum of its face maps. For a source-free move, the model supplies a compact chain $V$ in $M\\setminus C$ with $\\partial V=\\Sigma_1-\\Sigma_0$. For a move past the line, it supplies a compact chain $V$ in $M\\setminus C$ with boundary $\\Sigma_1-\\Sigma_0-\\sum_j\\epsilon_jS_j^2$, where each $S_j^2$ is a small oriented normal two-sphere around a transverse intersection of the swept support with $C$ and $\\epsilon_j$ is its sign; transverse means the tangent spaces of the 3-chain and $C$ span $T_xM$ at the intersection. Set $I(V,C)=\\sum_j\\epsilon_j$. The claimed action is that a source-free move leaves $U_\\alpha$ unchanged, while a move across the line multiplies it by $e^{i\\alpha m I(V,C)}$. In particular, the line carries the character $\\chi_m(e^{i\\alpha})=e^{i\\alpha m}$ of the magnetic one-form $U(1)$ symmetry.",
